# meal-planner-web (React PWA)

Shared `docs/` (ARCHITECTURE.md, ROADMAP.md, STATUS.md) live in the `meal-planner-api` repo, not here. Read them there before starting work — `../meal-planner-api/docs/` if checked out as a sibling, otherwise pull current versions from that repo on GitHub.

## Before doing anything
Read, from `meal-planner-api`'s docs: `STATUS.md` (actual current state — wins on conflicts), `ARCHITECTURE.md` (stack, data model, system design, §5 for the type-generation workflow this repo depends on), `ROADMAP.md` (the phase plan).

## Conventions
- Terse, self-documenting code. No gold-plating, no speculative abstraction for features not yet in the current phase.
- Stage changes; don't commit unless explicitly told to.
- Never hand-edit `src/types/api.d.ts` or `src/types/api.zod.ts` — they're generated from the API repo's OpenAPI spec via the `generate:types` script. Regenerate, don't patch.
- Validate API responses through the generated Zod schemas at the network boundary rather than trusting TS types alone.
- Deviations from ARCHITECTURE.md or ROADMAP.md should be noted for the user to carry into `meal-planner-api`'s `docs/STATUS.md` — this repo doesn't hold its own status log by design, to avoid two conflicting sources of truth.

## End of session
Flag in chat anything completed, in progress, or decided, and whether a type regen is needed and wasn't run.
